    "body": "> > Another option would be to install to `~/bin` or `~/.local/bin` by default.\r\n> \r\n> Checking locally, I don't see those paths added to `$PATH` by default, so it may require users having the add new paths to their `$PATH`. I think we should avoid raising the barrier to use Starship if possible.\r\n\r\nTrue, it's less commonly included by default. On the other hand it doesn't really need to be in the `$PATH` at all for inclusion in the shell profile (absolute paths). I agree that existing paths should be preferred though.",
